[$in title:["Template directives"]]
[$in description:["A reference to all Moth template directives, with examples of slots, child wrappers, comments and text formatting."]]
[$in head:[language_theme_head]]

[navbar]
[sidebar]
listed = sync_navigation(sidebar_id)!
[section, $md:
    # Template directives

    A template directive changes how one bracket construction builds its result.
    Write its name in the head, before the colon. A slot can collect contributions
    from a caller, a wrapper can repeat markup around children and a formatter
    can turn authored text into HTML.

    - @#directive-heads (Head syntax and comments) covers commas, operands and `$note`.
    - @#slot-directives (Slots and inserts) covers `$slot`, `$in` and `$supplied`.
    - @#child-wrapping (Wrapping direct children) covers `$before`, `$after` and `$fresh`.
    - @#text-formatters (Text formatters) covers `$raw`, `$md`, `$html`, `$escape_html`, `$css` and `$code`.
]

[section:
